# Git commits

Follow [Conventional Commits 1.0.0](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/en/v1.0.0/).

## Format

```
<type>[optional scope]: <description>

[optional body]

[optional footer(s)]
```

- Type and description are required; colon and space after type/scope.
- Description is a short summary in imperative mood (e.g. `add`, `fix`, `update`).
- Body (if any) starts one blank line after the description.
- No emoji in commit messages.

## Types

| Type | Use when |
|---|---|
| `feat` | New user-facing capability |
| `fix` | Bug fix |
| `docs` | Documentation only |
| `style` | Formatting; no code change |
| `refactor` | Restructuring without behavior change |
| `perf` | Performance improvement |
| `test` | Tests only |
| `build` | Build system or dependencies |
| `ci` | CI configuration |
| `chore` | Maintenance that does not fit above |

## Breaking changes

Indicate with `!` after type/scope and/or a footer:

```
feat(api)!: drop legacy share token format

BREAKING CHANGE: share URLs created before v2 no longer resolve.
```

## Attribution — never add Cursor trailers

- Do **not** add `Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>` or any other `Co-authored-by` / `Co-Authored-By` trailer.
- Do **not** add "Made with Cursor" or similar agent attribution footers.
- Commit author stays the human user; message body describes the change only.

## Examples

```
feat(web): show history and share buttons on document edit page

fix(backend): return 404 when folder permission is missing

docs: document folder permission inheritance

test(web): cover history-share button visibility
```
